[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is centered with generous negative space, presented from a 3/4 overhead angle (40°) to clearly show the textures of the dip, pita, and cucumber. A shallow depth of field keeps the foreground plate sharp while the background blurs softly. Soft, natural side light from a window on the left creates subtle highlights on the dip and gentle, realistic shadows. The setting is a rustic kitchen featuring an aged oak wood surface with visible grain. The dip is a smooth, creamy, vibrant sunset-orange puree served in a simple matte ceramic bowl, positioned slightly to the left on a neutral stone platter. Arranged naturally beside the bowl are two portions of thick-cut, crisp cucumber rounds and toasted whole-wheat pita wedges, placed side-by-side without stacking. A worn wooden spoon rests casually on the surface near the plate, with a few stray crumbs of pita and a single walnut half scattered nearby to imply preparation. The dip shows a rich, uniform texture with tiny, subtle flecks of red pepper flakes and a slight sheen from the olive oil. The scene looks authentic, lived-in, and warm with a golden-hour color temperature. No green herbs, no parsley, no cilantro, no green garnish. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. Slight natural imperfections: a small smudge of dip on the bowl rim, uneven placement of the pita wedges. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional cookbook photography."
  }
]
